  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="1">Re-run the blast-radius grep: git grep -n -i "api/agent\|AgentEndpoints\|AgentModule\|AgentTokenService\|AgentTokenOptions\|Api\.Agent\|HandoffUrlBuilder" -- src/server tests ':!**/bin/**' ':!**/obj/**'; save the list to projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/notes/001-blast-radius.md.</step>
    <step order="2">In PlaybookAuthorizationFilter, remove the AgentPlaybookRequest branch of AuthorizeRunAsync and the agent-route doc comments (:48, :127, :541); grep for any other use of the two AgentEndpoints constants (move them only if one exists); in PlaybookRouteAuthorizationContractTests, delete the AgentRunPlaybook_* tests and rewrite any Run-mode proof that exists only on the agent route against POST /api/ai/playbooks/{id}/execute; build.</step>
    <step order="3">Move HandoffUrlBuilder to Services/Ai/Handoff/, register it in the AI module that registers the chat tool handlers, update the namespace in DataverseCreateRecordHandler and every test that uses it, and move HandoffUrlBuilderTests beside it; build and run the DataverseCreateRecordHandler and HandoffUrlBuilder tests.</step>
    <step order="4">Delete Api/Agent/**, Infrastructure/DI/AgentModule.cs, Configuration/AgentTokenOptions.cs; remove AddAgentModule (Program.cs:232) and MapAgentEndpoints (EndpointMappingExtensions.cs:479-480 and :5 using); remove agent-only config keys from appsettings.template.json and agent-only branches/comments in the other BFF files listed.</step>
    <step order="5">Update ArchTests (ledger rows, ProvenByTest, SessionOwnership, ADR013, TenantIsolation guards), delete or rewrite the /api/agent/* contract, eval and seam tests per the ADR-038 constraint; delete tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Api/Agent/AgentConfigurationServiceTests.cs and AgentConversationServiceTests.cs.</step>
    <step order="6">dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ (0 warnings); dotnet test for Spaarke.ArchTests, the BFF unit tests and the touched integration folders.</step>
    <step order="7">Re-run the FR-01 grep exactly as the first acceptance criterion states it; every remaining hit is DecisionsTextSummary.cs:11 (task 020's); list hits elsewhere in the repo (task 002's or history) in the task notes.</step>
    <step order="8">Publish the BFF (Release) and record the publish-size delta against a fresh master build; run dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive.</step>
    <step order="9">Write notes/001-issue-comments.md (#1523 decision draft) and the PR Placement Justification text.</step>
    <step order="10">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="11">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any code outside Api/Agent/** (other than HandoffUrlBuilder's consumers and the two constants) depends at runtime on an Agent* type or an /api/agent/* route, STOP and escalate with the dependency list rather than relocating more code.</trigger>
    <trigger>If removing agent-specific branches would change a non-agent credential, token or authorization path (AuthorizationModule, OrderedCredentialClientProvider, IdentityConfigurationValidator), STOP and escalate (root CLAUDE.md §6: security-sensitive).</trigger>
    <trigger>If a ProvenByTest or guard test cannot be rewritten against a live route without weakening the proof, STOP and escalate to the main session for uac-r2 review.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>HandoffUrlBuilder (Api/Agent/HandoffUrlBuilder.cs) is the existing deep-link composer; the new file is the same class moved (CAPABILITY-INDEX: no row; grep "HandoffUrlBuilder" shows DataverseCreateRecordHandler.cs:229 as its live consumer). notes/reuse-scan.md "Legacy removal blast radius (FR-01)".</existing>
    <extension>No new behaviour: the class moves out of the folder being deleted so its live consumer keeps compiling; it cannot stay in Api/Agent/ because that folder is removed by FR-01.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Deleting Api/Agent/ without moving it breaks the BFF build and DI resolution of DataverseCreateRecordHandler, so the chat create-record tool fails at startup.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

