  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">git grep -i "api/agent\|AgentModule\|AgentTokenService\|CopilotAgent" -- src/server/api src/server/shared tests ':!tests/scripts' returns only Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Decisions/DecisionsTextSummary.cs:11 (left for task 020). tests/scripts is task 002's; the history comment in src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/E2EAcceptance/E2EValidationRunner.cs:33 ("REMOVED BY TASK 230b", customer-provisioning) is left unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ succeeds with 0 warnings and 0 errors.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Spaarke.ArchTests, the BFF unit tests and the touched integration test folders pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">PlaybookAuthorizationFilter has no agent branch; POST /api/ai/playbooks/{id}/execute keeps its exact 400/403/404 responses (PlaybookRouteAuthorizationContractTests' execute-route tests pass unchanged), and every Run-mode rule that was proven only on the agent route is now proven on the execute route.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">DataverseCreateRecordHandler resolves HandoffUrlBuilder from DI in the test host, and the HandoffUrlBuilder tests and data-mutation tests that use it pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: an in-process test host request to POST /api/agent/message returns 404 (route not mapped).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No ledger row, PermanentBasis or SweepFinding for a route outside /api/agent/* changed (diff review in the PR).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The PR records the publish-size delta (expected negative; total at or under 60 MB) and no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The PR description contains "Closes #2575"; notes/001-issue-comments.md holds the #1523 draft.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

